 "verification": {
  "status": "double-checked",
  "note": "Both tables parsed from the PDF text layer by word positions (a Total line and a Susceptible line per organism; columns from the Total lines, rotated headers rebuilt from characters); every cell then compared by eye with zoomed crops of the rendered pages (scale 5), and every printed percentage re-computed from its printed susceptible count and number tested, 2026-09-26. The archived PDF was re-downloaded and matched the census file byte for byte (MD5)."
 },
 "notes": "Annual hospital-wide antibiogram of AIIMS Bhopal for 2021 (Department of Microbiology): for each organism the number of isolates (n), and per drug the number tested and the number (percent) susceptible. No specimen or location split, so rows are spec all, set all; there are no isolate count tables and no printed grand total. The printed percentage (a whole number) is recorded with the number tested; where the printed susceptible count and number tested give a percentage more than 1 point away (or more susceptible than tested), the cell is marked as a conflict. Colistin is recorded as printed: most organisms show 0 (0%) susceptible, which the rules flag (CLSI has no susceptible category for colistin); E. coli and C. freundii print 6 (60%) of 738 and of 18, marked as conflicts. The S. aureus row is not split by methicillin; cefoxitin is the printed OXSF (cefoxitin screen) column. Archived copy used (the live site could not be reached): https://web.archive.org/web/20250216004457id_/https://aiimsbhopal.edu.in/AIIMSFiles/annexuredImage/Antibiogram_January-December_2021.pdf.",
 "issues": [
  "Second reader 2026-09-26: every cell re-read from the page images (scale 5, zoomed crops by column group) before comparing with the file: all 249 cells (printed percentage and number tested) and all 14 row n. The seeded sample of 62 cells (sample_cells.py) is part of this. 0 transcription errors, nothing corrected. The cells left out are right: C. freundii ceftriaxone printed 0 (0%) of 0 tested; P. mirabilis amoxicillin 9 tested with no result printed; the ticarcillin-clavulanate, CXMA and ICR columns as listed in excluded.",
  "Second reader: every printed count (percent) pair re-computed independently. The 17 conflicts are exactly the recorded cells more than 1 point off, and each is printed that way: E. coli colistin 6 (60%) of 738; E. cloacae complex cefepime 39 (22%) of 74, imipenem 45 (54%) of 86, levofloxacin 17 (46%) of 34, cefuroxime 2 (6%) of 52; C. freundii colistin 6 (60%) of 18; C. koseri ceftriaxone 2 (30%) of 4; S. Typhi ceftazidime 89 (73%) of 11 (73% fits 8 of 11); CONS ciprofloxacin 52 (21%), erythromycin 35 (15%), nitrofurantoin 284 (98%), levofloxacin 54 (21%) and linezolid 245 (80%) of 297, clindamycin 115 (43%) of 299; S. aureus oxacillin 112 (45%) of 206; E. faecalis high-level gentamicin 8 (26%) and teicoplanin 34 (100%) of 35.",
  "Second reader: the 17 other cells the validator does not keep (6 colistin 0% cautions, 11 intrinsic) are printed as recorded. Stray strokes over \"%)\" in four cells (P. aeruginosa piperacillin-tazobactam, P. mirabilis cefoperazone, CONS ciprofloxacin and gentamicin) do not touch the numbers."
 ],
